  "practice": [
    "Say আ three times with an open, steady sound: a, a, a.",
    "Read each vocabulary word aloud and listen for আ at the beginning.",
    "Contrast অ (ô) with আ (a): অজগর (ôjogor), আম (am).",
    "Write আ five times, noticing that it resembles অ with an added vertical stroke on the right."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "আ is the second independent vowel in the Bengali alphabet. It has an open a sound, similar to the vowel in “father.”",
    "When আ follows a consonant, it usually becomes the vowel mark া (আ-কার): ক + া = কা (ka).",
    "Keep আ distinct from the shorter অ sound. Compare আম (am, mango) with অল্প (ôlpo, a little). Use the audio controls to imitate a Bengali voice."
  ]
